sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    participant Caller as a scenario<br/>src/todo/command/middleware/unit_of_work/test/nested_commands_steps_test.py
    participant Middleware as UnitOfWorkMiddleware<br/>src/todo/command/middleware/unit_of_work/middleware.py
    participant Import as ImportItemsHandler<br/>src/todo/command/import_items.py
    participant Add as AddItemHandler<br/>src/todo/command/add_item.py
    participant Repository as postgres.Repository of ItemRow<br/>src/todo/infrastructure/postgres/repository.py
    participant Unit as UnitOfWork, the router<br/>src/todo/infrastructure/postgres/unit_of_work/unit_of_work.py
    participant DB as PostgreSQL

    Caller->>+Middleware: handlers.import_items.handle(ImportItemsCommand)
    Middleware->>Unit: begin(): a new unit in the context, this command ends it
    Middleware->>+Import: call_next
    loop one nested AddItemCommand per title, through the decorated AddItem
        Import->>+Add: handle: the middleware calls begin, None, and passes on
        Add->>+Repository: insert(ItemRow), through ItemLists
        Repository->>+Unit: Database.session asks connection_for(write=True)
        Note over Unit,DB: the first write takes a connection and BEGIN
        Unit-->>-Repository: the unit's connection: the call runs behind a SAVEPOINT
        Repository->>+DB: INSERT
        DB-->>-Repository: the row, or 23505: ROLLBACK TO SAVEPOINT
        Repository-->>-Add: None, or DuplicateKeyError told as a conflict
        Add-->>-Import: result, or the conflict
    end
    Import-->>-Middleware: result, or the conflict
    alt the handler returned
        Middleware->>+Unit: unit.commit(), shielded from the caller's cancellation
        Unit->>DB: COMMIT
        Unit-->>-Middleware: None, or a failure told as unavailable
    else the handler raised
        Middleware->>+Unit: unit.rollback(), shielded
        Unit->>DB: ROLLBACK
        Unit-->>-Middleware: done
    end
    Middleware-->>-Caller: the result, or the failure
